 "segments": [
  {
   "id": 0,
   "start": 0.72,
   "end": 5.02,
   "text": " Every digital device, from a phone to a robot vacuum, runs on the same four-step loop."
  },
  {
   "id": 1,
   "start": 5.28,
   "end": 10.84,
   "text": " First, input sensors like a keyboard, microphone, or camera turn the physical world into electrical"
  },
  {
   "id": 2,
   "start": 10.84,
   "end": 17.3,
   "text": " signals. Second, processing. The CPU or central processing unit does the math and logic."
  },
  {
   "id": 3,
   "start": 18.18,
   "end": 26.22,
   "text": " Third, storage. Drive-second SSDs save data long-term. Fourth, output. Screens, speakers,"
  },
  {
   "id": 4,
   "start": 26.22,
   "end": 34.34,
   "text": " or motors turn digital results back into light, sound, or movement. Now why did our"
  },
  {
   "id": 5,
   "start": 34.34,
   "end": 39.24,
   "text": " 2 a.m. document vanish? Because a computer actually uses two very different places"
  },
  {
   "id": 6,
   "start": 39.24,
   "end": 46.44,
   "text": " to hold data. RAM and storage. Think of a computer as a kitchen. The CPU is the"
  },
  {
   "id": 7,
   "start": 46.44,
   "end": 53.16,
   "text": " head chef. Storage, your SSD, is the walk-in freezer down the hall. It holds a"
  },
  {
   "id": 8,
   "start": 53.16,
   "end": 59.62,
   "text": " huge amount of food, and if the kitchen lights go out, the food stays inside. RAM or Random"
  },
  {
   "id": 9,
   "start": 59.62,
   "end": 65.3,
   "text": " Access Memory is the chef prep counter right in front of them. The chef cannot chop vegetables"
  },
  {
   "id": 10,
   "start": 65.3,
   "end": 70.5,
   "text": " inside the freezer, so whenever you open a photo or a document, the computer copies it"
  },
  {
   "id": 11,
   "start": 70.5,
   "end": 79.56,
   "text": " from the SSD onto the RAM prep counter. RAM is thousands of times faster than an SSD."
  },
  {
   "id": 12,
   "start": 79.56,
   "end": 85.6,
   "text": " but there's a catch. RAM is volatile. It holds data as tiny electrical charges"
  },
  {
   "id": 13,
   "start": 85.6,
   "end": 90.36,
   "text": " that vanish the instant power drops. Until you press save to copy your work"
  },
  {
   "id": 14,
   "start": 90.36,
   "end": 95.56,
   "text": " from the RAM, counter back into the SSD freezer. A power cut wipes the counter"
  },
  {
   "id": 15,
   "start": 95.56,
   "end": 95.92,
   "text": " clean."
  }
 ],
